Anker all the way. There are different sizes (and thus, weight). The 10.000mah ones are super portable, the 22-23.000mah ones are heavy duty, will charge a MacBook, iPad, Switch, you name it. And then there are Anker MagSafe ones as well with much higher capacity than the Apple’s one.

I just bought this. Yes it’s overkill but it’s awesome: https://youtu.be/GDd6ufy45ZA Drop.com has it for $169.

I have an ESR 10000mAh Power bank. One important thing I’ll stress to you is make sure you ask is it MagSafe compliant? Not MagSafe compatible. Is it actually Apple MFI certified because if it’s not (like mine) it will only charge an iPhone at 7.5w wirelessly as opposed to 15w. It’s tricky because you read the specs and it says 18w capable but that’s Android charging.

I have the MagSafe battery pack and do note that’s it’s not for handling multiple charges, but more for ‘emergency’ use to top up your phone’s batt sufficiently enough for you to get to a proper charger. It only has over 1000mAh capacity. My main battery pack is a Mophie Powerstation 3XL with 26000mAh, more than enough juice for multiple charges.

